answer-field-6afd8803-48e7-5bb5-a8c7-f2cfa74acb78" :answer-field/id #uuid "6afd8803-48e7-5bb5-a8c7-f2cfa74acb78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e646b2c8-bef4-5c47-bd94-43b774f155f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2252249a-a2ef-500a-86d4-4161de85035c" "answer-e646b2c8-bef4-5c47-bd94-43b774f155f7" "answer-33a02670-7d41-54bc-beae-09bf0913a91b" "answer-fa535c76-36e8-571a-b86f-c71ade71e566" "answer-675f33f1-e90d-55b3-b156-b8e7db8663eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2252249a-a2ef-500a-86d4-4161de85035c" :answer/id #uuid "2252249a-a2ef-500a-86d4-4161de85035c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e646b2c8-bef4-5c47-bd94-43b774f155f7" :answer/id #uuid "e646b2c8-bef4-5c47-bd94-43b774f155f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33a02670-7d41-54bc-beae-09bf0913a91b" :answer/id #uuid "33a02670-7d41-54bc-beae-09bf0913a91b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa535c76-36e8-571a-b86f-c71ade71e566" :answer/id #uuid "fa535c76-36e8-571a-b86f-c71ade71e566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-675f33f1-e90d-55b3-b156-b8e7db8663eb" :answer/id #uuid "675f33f1-e90d-55b3-b156-b8e7db8663eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186139150 :question/problem "![](images/46/46c110dc92d254443f7046536f9384fc666d58109aada2cf78cbb1ce14c0a193.png)\n\nThe point shown above represents a number on a number line. The absolute value of this number is $5.$ What is the number?" :question/worked-solution "The number is *positive* because it is to the *right* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $5,$ so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $5.$ \n\nThe positive number at a distance of $5$ from zero is $5$\n\n![](images/7e/7e1e41b708d66f3b3abc1e58dd49afa96d958b64d6575bcdf7f6d26168bd13ba.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186137848 :answer-field/correct 17592186137851 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186139666 :tutorial/content "The **absolute value** of a number is its *distance from zero* when viewed on a number line. \n\nDistances are never negative. Therefore, the absolute value of a number is always positive or zero.\n\nLet's consider the number $-5$ and its position on a number line, shown below.\n\n![](images/30/3072e47752dc69d38f997e926092f60c24966031d0484241fa9c1133d89d1c56.png)\n\n \n\nThe **distance** between $-5$ and zero equals $5$ because $-5$ is five steps away from zero. \n\n![](images/dd/dd155b158a3457eb08a95885461d3ffbd36dd852e1b6c4e9dbda04efed749280.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, *the absolute value of * $-5$ *equals* $5.$ We write this as follows:\n\n$$\n| \\, {-5}  \\, |  = 5\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186139668 :tutorial/content "There is a fast way to find the absolute value of a number:\n\n- The absolute value of a positive number is equal to itself. For example, \n\n$$\n|8| = 8 .\n$$\n\n- To find the absolute value of a negative number, we drop the negative sign. For instance,\n\n$$\n| {-8} | = 8.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138603 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
